### Health
GET http://localhost:8080/health

### Get seeded business by documented ID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/businesses/biz_1

### Unknown business -> 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/businesses/does-not-exist

### List first page of reviews (newest first; response carries page/limit/total)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/businesses/biz_1/reviews?page=1&limit=2

### Second page - no record is skipped or repeated between pages
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/businesses/biz_1/reviews?page=2&limit=2

### Invalid paging -> 400 rather than a silently coerced page
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/businesses/biz_1/reviews?page=0

### Add review
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/businesses/biz_1/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{"user_id":"user_99","rating":5,"body":"Great place"}

### Get business again after creating review
### review_count and average_rating reflect the new review immediately
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/businesses/biz_1

### Invalid rating -> 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/businesses/biz_1/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{"user_id":"user_99","rating":9,"body":"Out of range"}

### Missing user_id -> 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/businesses/biz_1/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{"rating":5,"body":"Anonymous"}

### Google auth
### Needs GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID set and a token whose audience matches it.
### Without valid credentials this returns 401 (bad token) or 502 (provider
### unreachable). The verifier is covered end to end by the tests in
### internal/auth and internal/api instead.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/google
Content-Type: application/json

{"id_token":"replace-with-test-token"}

### Initialize subscription
### Needs PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY. Point PAYSTACK_BASE_URL at a local stub to try
### this without calling Paystack. The response reference is what correlates
### the later webhook back to this user.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/subscriptions/initialize
Content-Type: application/json

{"user_id":"user_99","email":"candidate@example.com","plan_code":"PLN_mock","amount":500000}

### Read subscription
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/subscriptions/user_99

### Webhook
### The signature is HMAC-SHA512 of the exact request body, keyed with
### PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY, so it cannot be written by hand. Generate one with:
###
###   BODY='{"event":"charge.success","data":{"id":42,"reference":"<reference>","status":"success","customer":{"email":"candidate@example.com"},"plan":{"plan_code":"PLN_mock"},"metadata":{"user_id":"user_99"}}}'
###   SIG=$(printf '%s' "$BODY" | openssl dgst -sha512 -hmac "$PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY" | awk '{print $2}')
###   curl -i -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/subscriptions/webhook \
###     -H "Content-Type: application/json" -H "x-paystack-signature: $SIG" -d "$BODY"
###
### Replace <reference> with the reference returned by the initialize call.
### Sending the same body twice is safe: the second delivery is acknowledged
### but not applied again.

### Webhook with no signature -> 401
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/subscriptions/webhook
Content-Type: application/json

{"event":"charge.success","data":{"id":42,"reference":"maoni_user_99_1","status":"success"}}
